---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const noList = [
  '"Just exploring AI" projects with no operational anchor',
  'strategy decks that are meant to substitute for implementation',
  'automation for its own sake',
  'teams optimizing for optics, novelty, or tool collection',
  'long timelines with no pressure to ship an artifact',
  'situations where nobody involved can actually decide anything'
];
---

<BaseLayout title="No List - hellointernet.lol">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <section class="cg-panel page-hero">
      <div class="cg-kicker">boundary conditions</div>
      <h1>No is part of the system.</h1>
      <p>
        This is not posture. It is load-bearing. A clean filter keeps the work honest and prevents preventable waste on both sides.
      </p>
      <div class="cg-meta">
        <span class="cg-status in-progress">selective by design</span>
        <span class="cg-status active">artifact pressure required</span>
        <span>if this bothers you, it is probably doing its job</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cg-card page-card">
      <div class="cg-kicker">default rejections</div>
      <ul class="bullet-list">
        {noList.map((item) => (
          <li>{item}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="page-grid tight">
      <article class="cg-card page-card">
        <div class="cg-kicker">translation</div>
        <h2>I do not want to be your AI mascot.</h2>
        <p>If the goal is symbolic adoption, trend compliance, or internal theater, I am the wrong person.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="cg-card page-card">
        <div class="cg-kicker">preferred condition</div>
        <h2>Real friction beats polished certainty.</h2>
        <p>A messy problem with authority to act on it is better than a clean brief that never intends to move.</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
